# Two classes stand in a function that runs three times, and every member captures: each evaluation has holders and closures of its own. A static field lies under the name of a static method above, and a static block lays a name.
# Members of the second evaluation alone are stored over in sight, on both sides; the first and the third keep theirs.
# A class without a member is evaluated three times as well: from the second time on its holders are made from the structures that the first left behind. A name is laid on a prototype object of the second and on the class object of the third.
# RUN: run-in-shell
# CHECK: field 1 kind 2 label 3 3 run 2
# CHECK-NEXT: kind 1 stored kind kind 3
# CHECK-NEXT: run 1 stored run run 3
# CHECK-NEXT: base 1 stored make base 3 field 2
# CHECK-NEXT: undefined say undefined undefined undefined make
# CHECK-NEXT: true false true true true
# CHECK-NEXT: exited with 0
# RUN(CALLED): run-in-shell mechanisms=all-Inlining
# CALLED: field 1 kind 2 label 3 3 run 2
# CALLED-NEXT: kind 1 stored kind kind 3
# CALLED-NEXT: run 1 stored run run 3
